{title: 050 - Abide With Me}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Worship}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Eb]Abide [Bb7]with [Cm]me; [Eb/G]fast [Ab]falls [Bb]the [Cm]e [Bb7/D]ventide;
[Eb]The [Ab/C]darkness deepens; [Fm]Lord, [Bb/D]with [Eb]me [Cm]abide!
[Eb]When [Gm/Bb]other [Cm]helpers [Ab]fail, and comforts [Fm]flee,
[Bb7/Ab]Help [Gm]of [Bb7/F]the [Eb]helpless, [Cm]Oabide [Eb/Bb]with [Bb]me!

Verse 2:
[Eb]Swift to [Gm/Bb]its [Bb7]close [Cm]ebbs [Eb/G]out [Ab]life's [Cm]little [Eb]day;
[Eb]Earth's [Ab/C]joys [Eb/Bb]grow [Ab]dim; [Eb]its [Fm]glories [Eb]pass [Cm]away;
[Eb]Change [Gm/Bb]and [Bb7]decay [Eb/G]in [Ab]all around [Cm]I [Fm]see;
[Bb7/Ab]O [Gm]Thou [Bb7/F]who [Eb]changest [Cm]not, [Ab]abide [Bb]with [Eb]me.

Verse 3:
[Eb]I need [Gm/Bb]Thy [Bb7]presence [Eb/G]every [Cm]passing [Eb]hour.
[Eb]What but [Ab/C]Thy [Eb/Bb]grace [Ab]can [Eb]foil [Fm]the [Bb/D]tempter's [Cm]power?
[Eb]Who, [Gm/Bb]like [Bb7]Thyself, [Eb/G]my [Ab]guide and stay [Cm]can [Fm]be?
[Bb7/Ab]Through [Gm]cloud [Bb7/F]and [Eb]sunshine, [Cm]Lord, [Ab]abide [Bb]with [Eb]me.

Verse 4:
[Eb]I [Gm/Bb]fear [Bb7]no [Cm]foe, [Eb/G]with [Ab]Thee [Bb]at [Cm]hand [Bb7/D]to [Eb]bless;
[Eb]Ills [Ab/C]have [Eb/Bb]no [Ab]weight, [Eb]and [Fm]tears [Bb/D]no [Eb]bitterness.
[Eb]Where [Gm/Bb]is [Bb7]death's [Cm]sting? [Eb/G]Where, [Ab]grave, thy victory?
[Bb7/Ab]I [Gm]triumph [Bb7/F]still, [Eb]if [Bb7]Thou [Cm]abide [Eb/Bb]with [Bb]me!
